# Expert-First: Research Required When User Expresses Doubt

## When This Gate Fires

STOP and fetch registered docs before making ANY response when the user:

- Says "I don't know", "I'm not sure", "I'm confused", "I'm a newbie", "I don't understand"
- Asks "how do I", "what's the right way", "what's the pattern for", "is this correct"
- Asks a question they cannot verify the answer to themselves
- Asks for explanation, guidance, expert opinion, or best practices on any topic
- Says they've been doing something "on my own" or "figured this out myself"
- Expresses any uncertainty about whether their current approach is right

## Required Actions — Before ANY Response

1. Open `.cursor/config.json` and enumerate the `docs` array
2. Identify which registered docs are relevant to the question
3. Fetch ALL relevant docs using `WebFetch` with the registered URL
4. Declare what was researched — one line per item (see format below)
5. Ground every recommendation in the fetched docs with explicit citations

## Research Declaration Format — MANDATORY

Every response that involved fetching must include this block:

> **Researched:**
> - `<doc-name>` — <one-line summary of what it says about the topic>
> - `<doc-name>` — <one-line summary>

This block must appear before the answer, not after. The user must know what was consulted
before reading the recommendation.

## Prohibited Before Research Completes

- Answering from training recall ("Typically in Ansible...", "Usually you would...")
- Using another project role as the primary answer (project files are examples, not authority)
- Producing any plan, direction, or implementation before docs are fetched and read
- Skipping the research declaration

## Why This Rule Exists

When the user says "I don't know", they are signaling:

> "I cannot verify your answer. I need you to actually know this, not guess."

In that moment, a confident training answer is still a training answer — not expertise.
The only acceptable response is grounded in authoritative docs: fetched, read, and cited.

## Registered Docs Reference

All available docs are in `.cursor/config.json` under `docs`. Key sources for common topics:

| Topic | Docs to fetch |
|---|---|
| Inventory, groups, host classification | `ansible-inventory-guide`, `ansible-host-group-vars`, `ansible-tips-tricks` |
| Variable scope and precedence | `ansible-variable-precedence`, `ansible-general-precedence` |
| Role design and structure | `ansible-roles` |
| Tags, playbook patterns, best practices | `ansible-tips-tricks`, `ansible-builtin-collection` |
| Windows/WinRM tasks | `ansible-windows-collection`, `community-windows-collection` |
| Any Ansible question | `guidelines://ansible-content-best-practices` via FetchMcpResource |
